// std.log: messages on stderr. All three are built into the compiler, because
// Aye has no variadic functions:
//
//     std.log.err(format, args...)    writes "error: <message>\n"
//     std.log.info(format, args...)   writes "info: <message>\n"
//     std.log.line(format, args...)   writes "<message>\n", no prefix
//
// `format` is a string literal; each `{}` in it is replaced by the next
// argument: an integer, float, bool, []u8 or error value (its name).
